WEBVTT

00:00.450 --> 00:02.911
This is Part 2: plan the job.

00:02.861 --> 00:05.419
Three formulas, five numbers.

00:05.419 --> 00:09.030
That's all you need, and you do it at the quote, not on the roof.

00:09.986 --> 00:12.158
Start with the power triangle.

00:12.108 --> 00:14.561
Watts equal volts times amps.

00:14.561 --> 00:18.717
Twenty-four volts times three point two amps is seventy-seven watts.

00:18.717 --> 00:21.298
Amps equal watts divided by volts.

00:21.298 --> 00:25.615
Seventy-seven watts divided by twenty-four volts is three point two amps.

00:25.615 --> 00:27.698
That's the one you'll use most.

00:27.698 --> 00:31.390
Cover the one you want with your thumb, and what's left tells you what to do.

00:32.338 --> 00:34.209
Now the five numbers.

00:34.159 --> 00:37.064
Fifty lights: aim for this on each circuit.

00:37.064 --> 00:39.807
Fifty-six lights: the most on a circuit.

00:39.807 --> 00:41.520
Never go past it.

00:41.520 --> 00:44.518
Three point two amps: the most on a circuit.

00:44.518 --> 00:47.180
That's eighty percent of a four amp breaker.

00:47.180 --> 00:50.802
Four hundred eighty watts: the most on a six hundred watt box.

00:50.802 --> 00:54.633
And twenty-two point eight volts: the lowest you want at the last light.

00:54.633 --> 01:00.143
Two more: one and a half lights per foot, and one point three seven watts per light on Pure White.

01:01.098 --> 01:02.575
Count lights.

01:02.525 --> 01:04.215
Never count feet.

01:04.215 --> 01:07.629
The old rule said inject every sixty to seventy feet.

01:07.629 --> 01:10.268
That's ninety to a hundred and five lights.

01:10.268 --> 01:12.178
Way too many amps.

01:12.178 --> 01:15.500
The first booklet said sixty lights, max seventy.

01:15.500 --> 01:18.416
That fills a four amp breaker right to the top.

01:18.416 --> 01:22.259
Now we inject every fifty lights, never more than fifty-six.

01:22.259 --> 01:25.338
At eight inch spacing, that's about thirty-three feet.

01:25.338 --> 01:27.398
Never past thirty-seven.

01:28.346 --> 01:31.154
Here's what one circuit pulls on Pure White.

01:31.104 --> 01:34.102
Forty lights: two point two eight amps.

01:34.102 --> 01:35.225
Good.

01:35.225 --> 01:40.445
Fifty lights: sixty-nine watts, two point eight five amps, about thirty-three feet.

01:40.445 --> 01:41.892
Aim here.

01:41.892 --> 01:46.023
Fifty-six lights: three point two amps, thirty-seven feet.

01:46.023 --> 01:47.574
That's the most.

01:47.574 --> 01:50.676
Sixty lights is three point four three amps.

01:50.676 --> 01:51.950
Stop.

01:51.950 --> 01:54.970
Ninety lights is five point one four amps.

01:54.970 --> 01:56.244
Stop.

01:56.244 --> 01:59.090
If the spacing changes, the feet change.

01:59.090 --> 02:01.185
The light count never does.

02:02.146 --> 02:04.399
Plan a job in four steps.

02:04.349 --> 02:06.490
All you need is the total feet.

02:06.490 --> 02:08.839
Take a hundred and fifty foot house.

02:08.839 --> 02:12.358
Step one: lights equal feet times one point five.

02:12.358 --> 02:14.812
That's two hundred twenty-five lights.

02:14.812 --> 02:19.013
Step two: circuits equal lights divided by fifty, rounded up.

02:19.013 --> 02:21.860
Four point five rounds up to five circuits.

02:21.860 --> 02:26.212
Step three: boxes equal circuits divided by five, rounded up.

02:26.212 --> 02:27.717
One box.

02:27.717 --> 02:29.870
Step four, the check.

02:29.870 --> 02:33.515
Two twenty-five divided by five is forty-five lights each.

02:33.515 --> 02:37.265
Forty-five times one point three seven is sixty-two watts.

02:37.265 --> 02:40.645
Divided by twenty-four, that's two point six amps.

02:40.645 --> 02:45.217
Forty-five is under fifty-six, and two point six is under three point two.

02:45.217 --> 02:48.758
The whole box is three hundred eight watts, under four eighty.

02:48.758 --> 02:50.008
Pass.

02:50.970 --> 02:53.315
Same house, the old way.

02:53.265 --> 02:55.488
Ninety lights on one circuit.

02:55.488 --> 02:59.353
Ninety times one point three seven is a hundred twenty-three watts.

02:59.353 --> 03:03.948
Divided by twenty-four, that's five point one amps, on a four amp breaker.

03:03.948 --> 03:05.222
Fail.

03:06.170 --> 03:08.006
Or use the quick table.

03:07.956 --> 03:10.236
Find the feet and read across.

03:10.236 --> 03:14.727
It uses fifty lights a circuit, and five circuits on a six hundred watt box.

03:14.727 --> 03:19.044
A hundred sixty-five feet is two hundred forty-eight lights on five circuits.

03:19.044 --> 03:21.151
That's the most for one box.

03:21.151 --> 03:24.299
Three hundred thirty feet is the most for two boxes.

03:24.299 --> 03:28.245
For track, feet divided by three point two eight gives metres.

03:28.245 --> 03:31.232
Each one metre piece holds about five lights.

03:31.232 --> 03:33.789
And order five percent extra lights.

03:34.738 --> 03:37.396
Check the controller before you count circuits.

03:37.346 --> 03:39.418
The board has six circuits.

03:39.418 --> 03:43.503
A single output controller uses one, which leaves five for injection.

03:43.503 --> 03:45.679
That's what the quick table uses.

03:45.679 --> 03:49.371
A PRO or PLUS controller uses five, leaving only one.

03:49.371 --> 03:51.350
You run out much sooner.

03:51.350 --> 03:53.862
Plan it at the quote, not on the roof.

03:54.810 --> 03:56.808
Two or more boxes?

03:56.758 --> 03:59.941
Put each box near its own GFCI plug.

03:59.941 --> 04:05.427
On a two box job, put them at opposite ends of the house, so each box covers its own part.

04:05.427 --> 04:07.753
Boxes never share a controller.

04:07.753 --> 04:09.374
Each has its own.

04:09.374 --> 04:12.441
Add both to the same app account so they work together.

04:12.441 --> 04:14.733
And test each box on its own.

04:15.698 --> 04:17.580
Parts to plan for.

04:17.530 --> 04:20.516
One T-injection at every injection point.

04:20.516 --> 04:23.514
Its feeder is thirty feet max of sixteen-two.

04:23.514 --> 04:27.507
Extensions for every gap, like doors, dormers and gables.

04:27.507 --> 04:29.023
Note the length.

04:29.023 --> 04:34.128
And signal boosters on any extension over ten feet, and at every jump to the second floor.

04:35.098 --> 04:37.385
Fill in the plan sheet at the quote.

04:37.335 --> 04:42.602
One row for each run: feet, lights, circuits, lights each, and amps each.

04:42.602 --> 04:44.338
Then the box check.

04:44.338 --> 04:51.687
Lights on the box times one point three seven must be under four eighty watts on a six hundred watt box, or under three sixty on a four fifty.

04:51.687 --> 04:53.481
Then count the parts.

04:54.450 --> 04:55.684
Recap.

04:55.634 --> 04:58.088
Watts equal volts times amps.

04:58.088 --> 05:01.317
Inject every fifty lights, max fifty-six.

05:01.317 --> 05:06.456
Three point two amps per circuit, max. Circuits are lights divided by fifty, rounded up.

05:06.456 --> 05:09.731
Boxes are circuits divided by five, rounded up.

05:09.731 --> 05:12.972
And one box covers about a hundred sixty-five feet.

05:13.922 --> 05:15.515
That's Part 2.

05:15.465 --> 05:18.405
Now take the Part 2 quiz in your training portal.
